    {
      "event": "text",
      "data": { "text": "## What failed\n\n[Run #12](piwi:run/12) failed 3 of its 48 tests, and the three " }
    },
    {
      "event": "text",
      "data": {
        "text": "belong to one failure cluster, [Cart total is stale after removing an item](piwi:cluster/3). The test checks the total before the cart call returns:\n\n1. It clicks **Remove** on the second item.\n2. It expects `cart-total` to read `$18.00` at once, while the request is still in flight.\n\nThe tool results name no [Run #99](piwi:run/99), so this answer says nothing about it."
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "block",
      "data": {
        "block": {
          "kind": "entity",
          "id": "run-12",
          "entity": { "type": "run", "id": 12, "label": "Run #12" },
          "status": "failed",
          "detail": "3 of 48 tests failed · main"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "block",
      "data": {
        "block": {
          "kind": "code",
          "id": "assertion",
          "title": "The check that fails",
          "language": "typescript",
          "code": "await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' }).nth(1).click();\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('cart-total')).toHaveText('$18.00');"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "event": "block",
      "data": {
        "block": {
          "kind": "patch",
          "id": "fix",
          "title": "Wait for the cart call before the check",
          "patch": "--- a/tests/cart.spec.ts\n+++ b/tests/cart.spec.ts\n@@ -14,5 +14,7 @@ test('removes an item', async ({ page }) => {\n   await page.goto('/cart');\n-  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' }).nth(1).click();\n+  const removed = page.waitForResponse((r) => r.url().includes('/api/cart') && r.request().method() === 'DELETE');\n+  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove' }).nth(1).click();\n+  await removed;\n   await expect(page.getByTestId('cart-total')).toHaveText('$18.00');\n });",
          "validation": { "status": "applies", "filesChecked": 1, "filesInPatch": 1, "errors": [] }
        }
      }
    },
